# SETTING the Oracle User Environment:
======================================
sudo su - oracle --> Switch to the operating-system oracle user. Oracle utilities use environment variables to determine which database instance and Oracle home you intend to manage.

Add the following variables to the end of ~/.bash_profile . Use an editor such as vi or nano: (to enable to them for every session)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
export ORACLE_BASE=/opt/oracle
export ORACLE_HOME=/opt/oracle/product/19c/dbhome_1
export ORACLE_SID=ORCLCDB
export PATH="$ORACLE_HOME/bin:$PATH"

Load the settings into the current shell and confirm them:
---------------------------------------------------------
source ~/.bash_profile
echo "$ORACLE_HOME" --> EXPECTED --> /opt/oracle/product/19c/dbhome_1
echo "$ORACLE_SID" --> EXPECTED --> ORCLCDB



